WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.950
Economists measured how American
drivers reacted to fuel prices

2
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:07.230
between 2001 and 2006.

3
00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.440
In the short run, a 10 per cent rise

4
00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.170
in price cut fuel use
by less than 1 per cent.

5
00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.920
Yet when a single brand puts up its price,

6
00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.970
its buyers can vanish.

7
00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.500
So why do some buyers barely
react when a price jumps,

8
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.950
while others switch away at once?

9
00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:28.170
In this mission, you'll measure
that reaction with one simple ratio,

10
00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.970
and learn five words for its size.

11
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:35.750
Then you'll reshape a demand curve
and predict how far sales move.

12
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.200
Your mission: find out what
decides how strongly buyers react.
